# Web UI (`web/`)

1. Read `.cursor/skills/react-pro/SKILL.md` before changing components or hooks.
2. Read `.cursor/skills/zero-web/SKILL.md` for repo scope (`web/src/**` only).
3. For visual work, follow `design-foundations` and `dark-mode` (CSS variables + `data-theme`).
4. For Next/RSC performance ideas, do **not** copy them here unless they apply to a client SPA. This app is React 18.2 + Vite + JSX.

## Must

- Function components; colocated sibling `.scss`
- State colocated; lift only when siblings share; Context only for rare writes
- Effects synchronize with external systems and clean up; user actions live in handlers
- `React.lazy` for heavy panels; no habit-memo (`useMemo`/`useCallback`/`memo` only for real cost or stable identity)
- Semantic HTML; `type="button"` on non-submit buttons; labeled inputs
- After UI changes, rebuild with `npm run build` when the operator needs `dist/web/`

## Must not

- Class components, mixins, `findDOMNode`, index keys on dynamic lists
- Copying props into state without `key={id}` reset
- Fetch waterfalls of sequential `await` when work is independent
- Polling when EventSource / `useRunStream` already exists
